<h1 id="the-rustgo-manual">The <em>Rustgo</em> Manual</h1>
<p>Welcome to <strong>rustgo</strong> -- a <code>Rust</code> compiler written in <em>Go</em>.
It supports <del>some</del> <strong>most</strong> of the language. See <a href="https://example.com/rustgo" title="Rustgo home">the repo</a>
or <a href="https://example.org/docs">https://example.org/docs</a>.</p>
<h2 id="getting-started">Getting started</h2>
<ol>
<li>Install Go</li>
<li>Build it:
<pre><code class="language-sh">go build -o rustgo ./cmd/rustgo
</code></pre></li>
<li>Run <code>rustgo file.rs</code></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>Fast <em>enough</em></li>
<li>Written in Go
<ul>
<li>with <strong>nested</strong> lists</li>
<li>and <code>code</code></li>
</ul></li>
<li>Escapes: *not emphasis* and 3 &lt; 4 &amp; 5 &gt; 2</li>
</ul>
